            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0741" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.51L9/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-25">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>303. Your 277, November 14, communicated to interested parties. Natural Products
                    Refining Company replies, “Need chrome ore to supply bichromates for reaching
                    [bleaching?], dyeing of cotton, also tanning. Quantity needed, 2,000 tons, so
                    small cannot affect supply for Army Navy purposes.”</p>
                <p>Add National Electrolytic company Niagara Falls, New York, to list in
                    Department’s of October 31.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d666-f1"/> Renew
                    representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
